<title>MEXICO: Mexico sugar czar sees 600,000 T exports in 1997.</title>
<headline>Mexico sugar czar sees 600,000 T exports in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexico sugar sector's top union leader predicted Wednesday that Mexico would produce a record 4.5 million tonnes this 1996-1997 harvest and export 600,000 tonnes from the crop.</p>
<p>The prediction of Enrique Ramos, the head of the mill workers' union, is in line with the National Sugar Chamber data and the National Association of Sugar Cane Growers.</p>
<p>Mexico's harvest runs from November to June, although from mid-May, tends to wind down. Peak output is in January and February.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
</text>
